;; FH-DIAG-002 — capability elision: the exact omitted-ViewCell count.
;;
;; A compiled declaration with no reactive site omits the reactive ViewCell
;; shell; one with a reactive site retains it. The verdict is a deterministic
;; function of the analyzed sites (EP-0036 D021), so the number of views that
;; omit the shell over a census of known cardinality is an exact integer.
;;
;; The census is `re-frame.freehand.manifest-views`: eight compiled views, five
;; without a reactive site (elided) and three with one (present) — two carrying
;; a committed event handler, one carrying a subscription. The count is five,
;; and it is asserted as an integer, never a threshold.
;;
;; `trusted-markup` is the row that makes the CAPABILITY / REACTIVITY split
;; visible. It carries a `(v/html s)` site, so its manifest claims the `:html`
;; capability and populates a roster — and it is still `:elided`, because the
;; verdict turns on reactive reads (`:sub`, a committed handler) and trusted
;; markup is neither. A declaration can therefore name a capability and prove
;; its ViewCell elidable at the same time.
{:fh/id "FH-DIAG-002"
 :omitted-view-cell-count 5
 :views {:label           :elided
         :card            :elided
         :list-view       :elided
         :mounts-label    :elided
         :trusted-markup  :elided
         :basket-total    :present
         :button          :present
         :two-buttons     :present}}
